Common Causes

1️⃣ No Internet / Unstable Network

Check first:

ping google.com

If this fails → your internet/DNS is down.

2️⃣ Broken DNS Configuration (Very Common on Kali/Linux)

Check your DNS file:

cat /etc/resolv.conf

If it’s empty or wrong → Recon won’t work.

A healthy example:

nameserver 8.8.8.8
nameserver 1.1.1.1

✅ Quick Fix (Recommended)

Edit DNS manually:

By typing the command: sudo nano /etc/resolv.conf

Replace content with:

nameserver 8.8.8.8
nameserver 1.1.1.1

Save → Exit.

Then restart networking:

sudo systemctl restart NetworkManager


After fix, run these diagonostic commands to verify fix


Try:

nslookup api.hackertarget.com

dig api.hackertarget.com


👉 OSINT & recon tools fail more from network misconfig than from “bugs”.

